  "worked_solution": "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=-2$ and $y=0.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below. Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, we use solid lines to divide the plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/975b596621dab7d455b09d75b1c8d2b9fd73e75cd2169ec40aadda48673f6883.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/9466a3fbf682ce967cda2294cfb61d5fa40b4f7c91686cfc8653cb4c1ffb4e97.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $(x+2)$ | ${y}^{3}$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(-3,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Top-Right | $(-1,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-3,-1)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(-1,-1)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n\n \n\nFinally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/b8e5807115c13aa842364a174058d1081bd84eba10dce13390da93832a1aeb54.png)",
